Notes on each fix, so you can review the intent:

1. `q93_scansSection_escapedOnce`: the old count over plain `text-center` cells and the `font-bold text-navy">$ESCAPED</td>` line pinned the old lab name cell and old scan cell layout, both gone. The test now pins the exact new notes cell content (`Fetuses / FHR / impression / BPD / HC / AC / FL` joined with ` · `), the EFW cell ending (escaped weight followed directly by the cell close, with no ` g` appended since the marker contains a letter), and keeps the photo badge assertion.
2. `q93_labsSection_escapedOnce`: keeps the exact new name cell markup verbatim as specified, asserts the result prints as `result space unit` escaped once, and checks the abnormal marker and its `val-abnormal` span with simple contains assertions instead of the old whole-span regex-shaped string; the old date cell line (`text-center text-muted`) pinned markup no longer listed, so it is dropped.
3. `q93_generatorOwnMarkup_stillPresent`: the only line that could no longer hold is the `mini-table` assertion, which belonged to the removed imaging appendix; it is replaced with a pin that the appendix text is gone. All other lines (risk badge, Current Medications, Delivery Plan, med-cell, photo badge, logo fallback, CLINICAL RECORD, section-title, table count) still match the new behaviour and are untouched.
